cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this case study, please cite it as below."
title: "Centromeric heterochromatin of Capra hircus: a sequence-based case study with public data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Alejo Herrador"
    given-names: "Tiago"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tiagoherrador/capra-hircus-centromeres"
keywords:
  - Capra hircus
  - centromere
  - satellite DNA
  - telomere-to-telomere assembly
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  A personal portfolio case study of the centromeric satellite DNA of public goat genomes.
  The T2T-goat2.0 assembly is the reference, 20 other public assemblies are screened against it,
  and the two animals with resolved centromeres are used to test the scaling of centromere
  length with chromosome size, satellite composition and differences between homologs, with an
  exploratory look at variation between breeds. Code under MIT; text and figures under CC BY 4.0.
